# The blocks below name no IdentityFile of their own, deliberately.
#
# They used to, and all eight of those paths were DANGLING — five under ~/.ssh/
# and three under a sibling directory that has never existed on this machine.
# ssh skips a missing IdentityFile silently, so they cost nothing at runtime and
# simply lied about where these hosts get their credentials.
#
# They get them from the AGENT: `Host *`'s IdentityFile plus whatever the agent
# is serving is the whole story. A host that needs one specific key pinned should
# name a PUBLIC key alongside IdentitiesOnly, the way github.com above does —
# never a private path that may or may not exist.
#
# Deliberately NOT replaced by naming the vault items that serve these hosts.
# This repo is PUBLIC, and which item unlocks which host is metadata worth not
# publishing — the same reason ssh-load-keys.sh keeps its manifest host-local.
